{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe mcp entrypoint skips cloning the tickets branch whenever `${REBAR_TRACKER_DIR}/.git` merely\nEXISTS. A `.git` directory is not proof of a usable clone, and the named volume PERSISTS across\ncontainers — so one interrupted clone poisons the store permanently. No later container\nre-clones, and the server serves an empty tracker forever.\n\n## Observed in production (2026-08-26)\n\nThe 120s blue-green health rollback removed containers mid-clone, repeatedly (that was bug\n`unfit-beneficial-whimbrel`). Each removal left the volume holding orphaned objects. The\nsurviving state:\n\n    du -sh $REBAR_TRACKER_DIR   ->  1.5G\n    ls $REBAR_TRACKER_DIR       ->  0 ticket directories\n    cat .git/HEAD               ->  ref: refs/heads/.invalid\n    ls .git/refs/heads          ->  (empty)\n    git rev-parse HEAD          ->  fatal: your current branch appears to be broken\n    rebar list (in container)   ->  []\n\n1.5 GB of objects, no worktree, no resolvable HEAD. Every subsequent container saw `.git`,\nskipped the clone, and served `[]`.\n\n## Why this is worse than a missing store\n\nThe absent-store guard (`antelopine-limivorous-chinchilla`) makes a MISSING store loud —\n`store_uninitialized`. A poisoned store reads as PRESENT, so the guard correctly does not fire\nand reads return `[]` again. The silent-empty failure mode is reintroduced through a different\ndoor: a store that exists, is empty, and has no connection to origin.\n\n## Fix\n\nRequire a RESOLVABLE HEAD before trusting the clone, and clear the directory before re-cloning\nso partial objects cannot poison the retry:\n\n    if ! git -C \"$DIR\" rev-parse --verify -q HEAD >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n      rm -rf \"$DIR\"/.[!.]* \"$DIR\"/*\n      git clone --single-branch --branch tickets \"$URL\" \"$DIR\" || echo \"clone deferred\" >&2\n    fi\n\nVerified against the exact production shape (`.git` present, HEAD -> refs/heads/.invalid, empty\nrefs/heads): the old guard SKIPS, the new one re-clones. A healthy store still resolves HEAD and\nis skipped, so no needless re-clone of a ~200k-commit branch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A tracker dir whose HEAD does not resolve is treated as unusable and re-cloned, not\n      trusted because `.git` exists.\n- [ ] The directory is cleared BEFORE the re-clone, so partial objects cannot survive into it.\n- [ ] A healthy store (resolvable HEAD) is still skipped — no re-clone on every boot.\n- [ ] Regression coverage pins the verify -> clear -> clone ORDER; clearing after the clone\n      would delete the fresh store.\n\n## Verification\n\n    .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py \\\n                              tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py -q -p no:randomly\n\nTeeth (each verified by re-introducing the defect and watching the test return to RED):\nreverting the gate to the `.git`-existence check turns\n`test_poisoned_store_with_dot_git_but_no_resolvable_head_is_cleared_and_recloned` RED;\ndropping the double-check turns\n`test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone` RED;\nremoving the safety guard turns `test_the_clear_refuses_an_unsafe_tracker_dir` RED.\n\n\n## Scope growth during implementation\n\n### 1. Extract the entrypoint into a real script\n\nThe entrypoint was generated inside `RUN { echo '...'; } > /usr/local/bin/mcp-entrypoint.sh`, so\nthe only possible test was a grep over Dockerfile source — a change-detector that cannot execute\nthe path it claims to pin. It moves to `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`, COPYed and installed,\nper the `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` precedent. `provision_store` becomes directly executable\nagainst a temp dir with a stubbed `git`.\n\n**The PAT gate and credential helper are RETAINED, not replaced.** The verify -> clear -> clone\npath stays inside the existing `if [ -n \"${MCP_TICKETS_PAT:-}\" ]` guard with its\n`credential.${MCP_TICKETS_URL}.helper` setup (the remote is private). Shape:\n\n    if [ -n \"${MCP_TICKETS_PAT:-}\" ]; then\n      git config --global \"credential.${MCP_TICKETS_URL}.helper\" '...'\n      if ! git -C \"$DIR\" rev-parse --verify -q HEAD >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n        acquire_lock || return 1        # see 2\n        clear_tracker_dir \"$DIR\"        # guarded; refuses empty / \"/\" / relative\n        git clone --single-branch --branch tickets \"$MCP_TICKETS_URL\" \"$DIR\"\n        release_lock\n      fi\n    fi\n\nA **PAT-less boot clears nothing and clones nothing** — it falls through exactly as today.\n\n### 2. Serialize the re-clone\n\nProvisioning is backgrounded (`provision_store &` then `exec \"$@\"`) because the ~200k-commit\nclone outruns the 120s readiness deadline. The deploy flock therefore serializes deploy TICKS\nbut NOT provisioning windows: `/health` answers before the store exists (see\n`mobile-groovy-badger`), autodeploy releases its lock mid-clone, and the 2-minute timer starts a\nsecond container which sees an unresolvable HEAD — because the first is still cloning — and\nclears the directory out from under it. Two further lock-free paths exist: compose `mcp:` carries\n`restart: always` on the same volume, and the client-PAT runbook prescribes a manual restart.\n\n**Protocol.** Lock is `${REBAR_TRACKER_DIR}.reclone.lock`, a regular file containing epoch\nseconds, written to a temp file and `ln`-ed into place so it is atomic WITH its timestamp — there\nis no window where the lock exists without a readable marker. `MCP_RECLONE_LOCK_STALE=7200`s and\n`MCP_RECLONE_LOCK_WAIT=7200`s, both deliberately far above any observed clone, so a slow-but-\nhealthy clone is never declared stale. Poll `MCP_RECLONE_LOCK_POLL=10`s.\n\n**The loser blocks; it does not skip.** On contention it polls up to `WAIT`, then RE-CHECKS HEAD\nafter acquiring: if the winner's clone landed, it returns WITHOUT re-cloning. If the budget\nexpires it returns non-zero so the failure is logged and the read guard reports\n`store_uninitialized` — it never silently `exec`s over an unresolvable store.\n\n**Alternatives weighed.** `flock` (repo prior art: `autodeploy.sh` `flock -n 9`,\n`_snapshot/git_fetch.interprocess_lock`) auto-releases on holder death and would make staleness\nmoot; it is the better primitive and is recorded as follow-up `beton-inversive-stag` rather than\ntaken here, because the tested implementation already exists and re-plumbing it is a larger\nchange than this bug warrants. Clone-to-temp-then-rename was also considered; it makes publish\natomic but doubles peak disk on a 1.5G store, which the box (root at ~80%) cannot absorb.\n\n## Additional acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `provision_store` is executable in tests against a temp dir with a stubbed `git`.\n      Proof: `pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py`\n- [ ] A PAT-less boot neither clears nor clones.\n      Proof: `test_no_pat_skips_the_clone_but_still_converges_the_store`\n- [ ] `clear_tracker_dir` refuses empty, `/`, or relative `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`.\n      Proof: `test_the_clear_refuses_an_unsafe_tracker_dir`\n- [ ] Two overlapping provisioning windows cannot both clear-and-clone.\n      Proof: `test_a_concurrent_reclone_is_not_interleaved`\n- [ ] The loser observes the winner's completed clone instead of re-cloning.\n      Proof: `test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone`\n- [ ] A container dying while holding the lock does not wedge the store.\n      Proof: `test_an_abandoned_lock_is_broken_rather_than_wedging_the_store_forever`\n- [ ] An unreadable lock marker is treated as abandoned, not as fresh.\n      Proof: `test_a_lock_with_an_unreadable_timestamp_is_treated_as_abandoned`\n- [ ] An unremovable stale lock exhausts the wait budget instead of hot-spinning.\n      Proof: `test_an_unremovable_stale_lock_exhausts_the_wait_budget_instead_of_spinning`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787796509395711001,"uuid":"89811f8f-97ae-4b84-a13b-83a9d6c9ab45"}